WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.827
RIGHT JOIN is valid PostgreSQL syntax and it preserves every row from the right table.

00:00:05.827 --> 00:00:11.297
In this example, departments is on the right, so every department stays even if no medical staff member

00:00:11.297 --> 00:00:14.627
belongs to it.

00:00:14.627 --> 00:00:19.807
If a department has no staff, the department information still appears and the staff columns become NULL.

00:00:19.807 --> 00:00:25.517
That makes it easy to identify empty departments.

00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:31.607
In practice, many analysts prefer LEFT JOIN because it reads more naturally from left to right.

00:00:31.607 --> 00:00:35.872
We could place departments first and then LEFT JOIN medical staff.

00:00:35.872 --> 00:00:42.162
The result would be easier for many people to read because the preserved population appears first.

00:00:42.162 --> 00:00:44.682
This is an important style lesson.

00:00:44.682 --> 00:00:47.262
SQL is not only for the computer.

00:00:47.262 --> 00:00:53.797
It is also documentation for the next analyst, developer, or data engineer who reads your work.

00:00:53.797 --> 00:00:58.067
The best join is often the one that makes the business meaning obvious.

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:04.002
So rather than memorizing RIGHT JOIN as a special case, focus on the preservation rule:

00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:06.033
which table must remain complete?
